":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'resolve_pinned_model(pass_name) resolves the model for each pass from the production class ... requires the resolved id to be a Bedrock id ... refusing (raising) when the resolved id is not a Bedrock id.'","Prior art: src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py:298 resolve_class, :335 resolve_model_string, :316 load_class_slots, :307 resolve_fallback_chain","Prior art: src/rebar/llm/config.py:247 split_provider_qualifier — 'THE single place that answers \"is this string provider-qualified?\"' and explicitly warns a bare ':' scan mis-splits canonical Bedrock ids ('...-v1:0')","Prior art (homogeneous single-provider chain concept): docs/ci-provider-matrix.md; model_classes.should_fall_back (deliberately-narrow failover); docs/local-dev-env.md 'deliberately does not fail over'"],"finding":"resolve_pinned_model's resolution and its 'is a Bedrock id' check reinvent existing rebar machinery rather than naming the prior art it should build on: model_classes.resolve_class/resolve_model_string/load_class_slots already turn a class name into a resolved provider:model id, and config.split_provider_qualifier is the SINGLE canonical answer to 'is this string qualified for provider X'. The plan does not commit to reusing them, risking a parallel resolver and a hand-rolled colon-scan for the Bedrock check.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0baf5b53d66379fc","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Pinned targets': resolve_pinned_model(pass_name)","norm_id":"nee68787cd965ec47","priority":0.0825,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future Bedrock model id containing a colon (e.g. '...-v1:0') fails a naive 'contains bedrock:' / colon-based check in a parallel resolver, silently mis-classifying the pinned model","The class table's env overrides / provider-qualifier resolution drift between parity.py's own resolver and model_classes.py"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Specify that resolve_pinned_model loads slots via mod